        "point": "negative first argument",
        "statement": "When the first argument x is negative, gcdA x y equals the negation of gcdA |x| y, following the convention that the Bézout coefficient is adjusted to maintain the identity gcd x y = x * gcdA x y + y * gcdB x y.",
        "note": "Canonical choice inherited from natural-number extended GCD."
      },
      {
        "point": "zero inputs",
        "statement": "When x = 0, gcdA 0 y = 0; when y = 0, gcdA x 0 = 1 for positive x and -1 for negative x; when both are 0, gcdA 0 0 = 0.",
        "note": "Degenerate cases where the Bézout identity degenerates are handled by the natural-number gcdA convention."
      }
    ]
  },
